    "durationMs": 1483367,
    "finalText": "Implementation complete and verified. The URL shortener is built with Spring Data JPA + Flyway + PostgreSQL:\n\n- **Endpoints**: `POST /links` (201/409/422), `GET /links/{code}` (200/404), `GET /r/{code}` (302 + atomic single click increment, 404), `GET /links` (ascending creation order, `items`/`total`); all errors return JSON with an `error` field\n- **Validation**: absolute http/https URL with host, codes matching `[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}`, malformed JSON → 422; submitted URLs stored/returned unchanged\n- **Persistence**: Flyway migration `V1__create_links.sql`, settings derived from `DATABASE_URL` in `start.sh` (no hard-coded credentials); verified data and click counts survive restart\n- **`sh start.sh`**: derives JDBC settings, migrates, and serves the jar in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`; README documents startup\n\nTest data was cleaned up, the server stopped, and port 8000 is free — ready for the automated suite."
  }
